amendments.description:
RED FIRST: rotate EVERY whole-set pin and frozen count to the new truth before any wiring.
Tree: the shared checkout is at 736291c4 or later. That is the PR #59 merge, which brought in main's #58 (`moe mcp --as-operator`). Re-measure any line below that has moved.
This row OWNS all seven test files listed here. Governor ruling comment-1204078f: amend, do not split. The cap is settings.taskSizing.maxDistinctFiles = 20; with the step-3 amendment this row owns 13 files.

THE RULE FOR EVERY NUMBER HERE (epic rail 3): run the leg and take the PRINTED expected-vs-received as authoritative. Never compute a count by hand or freeze one in advance: a concurrent kind-publishing row can move the same literal first. #58 already moved several of these counts.

1. apps/daemon/src/mcp-tool-allowlist.test.ts (re-measured at 736291c4):
- the hand-written `expectedExcluded` (:232 onward), with the kind in its sorted position;
- the length pin (:260);
- the count object `{ excluded, queries, vocabulary, wired }` (:285). excluded and vocabulary rise; wired does NOT, because an operator kind is excluded from the seats' MCP roster;
- #58's NEW partition arm (:295-304). It asserts `[...MCP_DELEGABLE_OPERATOR_KINDS, ...MCP_NEVER_DELEGATED_KINDS]` equals the exclusion exactly, and pins `{ delegable, never }` at :299-301. It goes RED as soon as the kind joins OPERATOR_PRINCIPAL_KINDS, and turns green only once step 3(5) classifies the kind. `never` then rises by one and `delegable` does not.
The derived partition arm at :158-168 needs no edit unless the leg says otherwise.

2. apps/daemon/src/daemon-command-vocabulary.test.ts:
- ROWS length and the unique-kind count (:360-361);
- `FAMILY_MAPS.REPOSITORY_RECOVERY.size` (:413). It is 1 today and moves when the kind joins that family;
- the OPERATOR_ONLY list (:318);
- `OPERATOR_PRINCIPAL_KINDS.size` (:465).
For the `declared` pin (:405), read it from the leg: an operator-only kind with a null agent capability should leave it unmoved.

3. apps/daemon/src/mcp-main.test.ts (re-measured at 736291c4):
- the hand-written `EXPECTED_EXCLUDED_COMMAND_KINDS` (:225 onward), which `EXCLUSION_CASES` derives from;
- the length pin (:273);
- the transport product (:275);
- the sort-equality (:276-280).
The never-delegated loop at :465 is derived; leave it alone.

4. apps/daemon/src/mcp-http/mcp-http-host.test.ts: change the frozen counts ONLY (:694, :696, :725). Its EXCLUSION_CASES list is derived. Do NOT add an `it(` block to this file: :624 counts its own `it(` blocks with `toHaveLength(16)`.

5. apps/daemon/src/daemon-command-registry-human-approver.test.ts:
- the hand-written `expectedExclusions` (:387-418): add the kind in sorted position, with a one-line reason in its neighbours' style;
- the length and sort-equality pins (:419-421).

6. apps/daemon/src/daemon-store-dependencies.test.ts: the exact sorted served-kind roster `registryKinds` (:840). The family-scoped arms at :1168 and :1288 must NOT move.

7. apps/daemon/src/gates-human-only-fence.test.ts: its band is /^(?:design|preview|release)\./, so repository.* falls outside it. Add the named arm DoD 4 requires, which classifies the kind as human-only, WITHOUT widening that band.

Run the seven files and confirm they go RED for the RIGHT reason: the new kind is missing from production. Quote one failing line per file.
